{
  "comment": "Upgrade journals and the one outcome both recovery readers must reach: Updater.exe (PackageInstaller RecoverLocked) and Install-Upgrade.ps1 -RecoverOnly. Each case is an install folder with this target and these operations; a prior of null means the update added the file. Hashes, paths and the backup set are made by each test. Backup files hold the prior contents unless a case overrides them (null: no backup). Expected files list every recorded path that should exist afterwards; any other is absent. journal: cleared (no journal left), setAside (moved to .failed) or kept. A case may override top-level journal fields (journal; a string \"@sha:<text>\" is the hash of <text>), wrap the journal text (journalText, where {journal} is the generated JSON), and put earlier evidence in the way of .failed (failed: directory, or held for a file open without delete sharing). inaccessible lists files (backup:<path> for a backup) whose status cannot be read during a first recovery, which must fail with every file and the journal unchanged; expect is the outcome of a second recovery once access returns.",
  "target": {
    "Launcher.exe": "new-launcher",
    "Updater.exe": "new-updater",
    "added.bin": "new-added",
    "skipped.dll": "same"
  },
  "operations": [
    { "path": "Launcher.exe", "prior": "old-launcher" },
    { "path": "Updater.exe", "prior": "old-updater" },
    { "path": "added.bin", "prior": null },
    { "path": "removed.txt", "prior": "old-removed" }
  ],
